[38;5;231m⏺[39m Here's the design.

  [1mApproach.[0m A single native [38;5;153m<input type="checkbox">[39m wrapped in a [38;5;153m<label>[39m, placed inside the existing empty [38;5;153m<main>[39m. The
  browser owns the checked/unchecked state entirely — no JavaScript, no attributes to manage, and it's
  keyboard-accessible and screen-reader-labeled for free by virtue of the wrapping [38;5;153m<label>[39m. Wrapping rather than [38;5;153mid[39m/[38;5;153mfor[39m
  avoids inventing an id and makes the text part of the click target.

  [1mMarkup[0m (replacing the empty [38;5;153m<main></main>[39m on line 9):

  [90m<[34mmain[90m>[39m
    [90m<[34mlabel[90m>[39m
      [90m<[34minput[90m [36mtype[90m=[31m"checkbox"[90m>[39m
      Example task
    [90m</[34mlabel[90m>[39m
  [90m</[34mmain[90m>[39m

  [1mOne judgment call to confirm:[0m I'd add a three-line [38;5;153m<style>[39m in the [38;5;153m<head>[39m that strikes through the label text when
  checked, using [38;5;153mlabel:has(:checked) { text-decoration: line-through; }[39m. Rationale: "mark items as done" implies you can
  see which are done, and the default checkbox alone is a small visual signal. It's supported in all current browsers.
  Say the word and I'll drop it — the checkbox works identically without it.

  [1mFiles touched.[0m [38;5;153mindex.html[39m only. Nothing else in the repo changes.

  [1mTesting.[0m This repo has no test infrastructure — no package.json, no runner, no existing tests — so there's no
  established pattern to extend, and I'm not proposing to introduce one for a static checkbox. Verification is manual:
  open [38;5;153mindex.html[39m in a browser, confirm the box toggles on click, on clicking the label text, and on Space when focused
  via Tab. I'll report what I actually observed rather than assert it works.

  [1mOut of scope,[0m flagging explicitly so it isn't a surprise: state does not persist across reload, and nothing else on
  the page can read whether the box is checked. Both need JavaScript, which the static-markup choice rules out.
  Straightforward to add later if you want them.

  Does this look right? I'll implement once you say yes — including whether to keep the strikethrough.

